# Patent Claim

**Claim 1:** A multilayer optical coating structure comprising:

a substrate having a surface upon which a plurality of optical layers are sequentially deposited via ion source-assisted vacuum deposition, said plurality of layers comprising:

a Layer A consisting essentially of silicon dioxide (SiO₂) having a refractive index in the range of 1.45 to 1.48 at a reference wavelength of 550 nm, deposited to a physical thickness of between 50 nm and 120 nm, wherein said Layer A is deposited using an ion source operating at an ion energy of between 80 eV and 150 eV to promote densification;

a Layer B disposed adjacent to said Layer A, consisting essentially of tantalum pentoxide (Ta₂O₅) having a refractive index in the range of 2.05 to 2.20 at said reference wavelength, deposited to a physical thickness of between 20 nm and 60 nm, wherein said Layer B is deposited using ion-assisted deposition at an ion beam current density of between 50 μA/cm² and 120 μA/cm²;

a Layer C disposed adjacent to said Layer B, consisting essentially of aluminum oxide (Al₂O₃) having a refractive index in the range of 1.60 to 1.70 at said reference wavelength, deposited to a physical thickness of between 30 nm and 80 nm, wherein said Layer C is deposited using an oxygen-argon ion source gas mixture at a ratio of between 1:3 and 1:5;

a Layer D disposed adjacent to said Layer C, consisting essentially of niobium pentoxide (Nb₂O₅) having a refractive index in the range of 2.25 to 2.40 at said reference wavelength, deposited to a physical thickness of between 15 nm and 45 nm, wherein said Layer D is deposited using ion-assisted deposition with substrate bias voltage maintained between −50 V and −150 V; and

a Layer E disposed adjacent to said Layer D, consisting essentially of magnesium fluoride (MgF₂) having a refractive index in the range of 1.37 to 1.39 at said reference wavelength, deposited to a physical thickness of between 90 nm and 130 nm, wherein said Layer E is deposited using ion source-assisted deposition at a chamber base pressure of less than 5 × 10⁻⁵ Torr prior to ion-assisted deposition initiation;

wherein said layers A through E are arranged in sequential order upon said substrate to form an alternating high-refractive-index and low-refractive-index layer stack, and wherein each of said layers A through E is deposited using a common ion source configured to bombard each respective layer material during physical vapor deposition to increase packing density and reduce moisture-induced refractive index shift of the resultant multilayer optical coating structure.

---

**Claim 2 (dependent):** The multilayer optical coating structure of claim 1, wherein said common ion source is a Kaufman-type or RF ion source operating with an inert gas selected from the group consisting of argon, xenon, and mixtures thereof, and wherein said ion source is further supplied with reactive oxygen gas during deposition of Layers B and D to achieve stoichiometric metal oxide formation.

**Claim 3 (dependent):** The multilayer optical coating structure of claim 1, wherein the total physical thickness of said layers A through E is between 300 nm and 450 nm, and wherein said multilayer optical coating structure exhibits an average reflectance of less than 0.5% across a wavelength band of 450 nm to 650 nm.
